        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-12T11:05:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would prefer not to do that in order to maintain the self-containment of the `requests` crate. Up until now, the `requests` crate has been solely responsible for validating the data in the `request` against a reference value (dice chain and vendor hash). It is quite decoupled from rialto actually.\n\nWhether the values are extracted from the DT or simply a fake is a decision made by rialto. Passing the DT would require the `requests` crate to make several rialto-specific decisions, such as determining which field should be used to read the vendor digest, which is mostly a contract between rialto and pvmfw. Similarly, in non-protected rialto, we would use a fake dice chain. I don\u0027t think the requests crate should be responsible for making these decisions.\n\nWe can group them in a struct like `ReferenceValue` if you think that\u0027s more clear.",
      "parentUuid": "50134a78_bd9e20c9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 182,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 182,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "0410b1128af934fdb8267d32637e0f977c37abd4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
